FINDINGS. #C924 deploy-over-ssh at 6beddbb0.
F1 (required): board-deploy.mjs takes the deploy and tree sha256 from the steps file on the same disk at run time, and the pasted one-liner checks only board-deploy.mjs. Today the pasted line carries the deploy file's own hash, the one Security signed, so what runs is bound to what was signed out of band. With this, anything that can write the owner's board folder (every agent can) could change board-store-deploy-pc<n>.mjs and its two hash lines in the steps file together, and it would run with the Cloudflare token in its environment. Fix: the pasted line carries both hashes (node board-deploy.mjs pc<n> <deploySha> <treeSha>), board-deploy.mjs refuses unless they match the files on disk (and the steps file, if you keep that check), and make-pair writes that line.
Holds, no change needed: loadCloudflare uses lstat (refuses a link or a folder), refuses a file under any .git and refuses group or other bits before reading, and names only the key, never the value. The token reaches only the migration and deploy spawns' environment, never argv and never the page-build spawn. stop(), hint() and the deploy output pass through redact(), including the unexpected-error path. The migration's inherited stdio is not redacted; wrangler does not echo its token, so that is accepted. scan.mjs refuses board.private.json by name, unread. Exposure: the token sits on a disk the agents' file tools can read, but wrangler's OAuth login already keeps an equivalent login (with a refresh token) at ~/Library/Preferences/.wrangler/config/default.toml, mode 600, same user, so that exposure is not new.
Recommendations (owner's, not blocking): create the API token with the least scope (Workers Scripts Edit and D1 Edit on the one account only) and an expiry date; add board.private.json to the agents' read-deny list in Claude settings (the owner's change, not an agent's); the one-liner still uses cd and relative paths, against #C921.
